  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capability Fund initiatives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This component will set up a capability fund to invest in supporting bespoke and innovative offers in the sector which are working to drive up both prevention and response practices and standards.

It will support: ?
Unique, essential sector services to raise and meet operational standards, with a view also to building more survivor-centred approaches that prioritise the safety and dignity of those we serve. ?
Targeted SEAH resources with a focus on prevention (e.g. adherence to international standards), and response activities (e.g. SEAH training, communication and engagement activates).?
Piloting new, small-scale approaches to improve capability to meet standards and promote effective implementation across the sector.</narrative>
  </description>
